      "blocks": {
        "text_Bx49xA": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h2><strong>Label Shapes,</strong> <strong>Sizes, And Colors</strong></h2><p>Most vinyl labels are designed to deliver clear, functional information, which is why <strong>white vinyl</strong> is commonly used—especially for barcodes and safety messaging. However, NADCO can print vinyl labels in <strong>nearly any color</strong> to meet branding, identification, or compliance requirements.</p><p>Vinyl labels are available in:</p><ul><li>Small, large, and custom sizes</li><li>Standard and custom shapes, including:<br/>  Squares and rectangles<br/>  Circles and ovals<br/>  Arrows, hexagons, and specialty shapes</li></ul><p>They are ideal for <strong>die-cutting</strong> and precision applications.</p><h2><strong>Specialty Vinyl Labels</strong> <strong>Options</strong></h2><p>In addition to standard vinyl labels, NADCO offers specialty solutions designed to enhance safety and visibility:</p><ul><li><strong>Glow-in-the-dark vinyl labels</strong> for emergency egress and low-light conditions</li><li><strong>Reflective vinyl labels</strong> for improved visibility in dark or high-risk environments</li><li><strong>Anti-slip (ASV) vinyl</strong> featuring a thick, textured surface for traction and slip resistance</li></ul><p>These specialty options expand vinyl’s role beyond identification into active safety support.</p>",
            "subtext_color": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "text_Bx49xA"
      ],
